## Anti Patterns

### 1. String Concatenation

```typescript
// Không nên - unstructured logging
console.log('User ' + userId + ' created order ' + orderId);

// Nên - structured logging
logger.info({ userId, orderId }, 'User created order');
```

### 2. Logging Sensitive Data

```typescript
// Không nên - logging sensitive data
logger.info('User login', { password: req.body.password });

// Nên - sanitize
logger.info('User login', { email: req.body.email });
```

### 3. Excessive Logging

```typescript
// Không nên - too much logging
for (const item of items) {
    logger.info(`Processing item ${item.id}`); // Too verbose!
}

// Nên - summary logging
logger.info({ itemCount: items.length }, 'Processing items');
```

### 4. No Context

```typescript
// Không nên - no context
logger.error('Operation failed');

// Nên - rich context
logger.error({
    operation: 'processOrder',
    orderId: order.id,
    error: err.message,
    stack: err.stack
}, 'Operation failed');
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Consistent Field Names

```typescript
// Standard field names
const standardFields = {
    // Request context
    requestId: 'correlation-id',
    userId: 'user-id',
    sessionId: 'session-id',

    // Business context
    orderId: 'order-id',
    productId: 'product-id',
    transactionId: 'transaction-id',

    // Performance
    duration: 'duration-ms',
    latency: 'latency-ms',

    // Errors
    errorCode: 'error-code',
    errorMessage: 'error-message',
    stackTrace: 'stack-trace'
};
```

